CodeMixTax
==================

This repository contains two distinct bodies of work with different provenance.
Please preserve this file when redistributing.


1. Derived work (this fork) -- MIT License, see LICENSE
-------------------------------------------------------
The evaluation pipeline for local/open-weight models:

    src/cmb_indic/**        configs/**        scripts/**
    tests/**                docs/**          results/**
    runs/**                 Makefile         pyproject.toml
    README.md

Relicensing note: upstream CodeMixBench is Apache-2.0. Apache 2.0 section 4
permits distributing a derivative work under different terms provided the
original notices are retained, so this fork's own contributions are offered
under the MIT License while the retained upstream files (item 2) stay under
Apache 2.0. The Apache text is preserved as LICENSE.upstream-Apache-2.0 and
continues to govern those files.

The metric implementations in `src/cmb_indic/metrics.py` are faithful ports of
`compute_token_label_Metric`, `compute_sentence_label_Metric` and `compute_BLEU`
from the upstream `utils.py` (see item 2), refactored to be side-effect free.
Scores produced by this pipeline are therefore directly comparable to the
upstream implementation for those metrics. Deviations are enumerated in
docs/DEVIATIONS.md.


2. Upstream CodeMixBench -- Apache License 2.0, retained unmodified
-------------------------------------------------------------------
These files are NOT covered by this fork's MIT license. They remain under the
Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE.upstream-Apache-2.0).
    utils.py                test_model.py    oaib/
    prompt.json             pics/            requirements.txt
    docs/upstream_README.md (the original README.md)

Upstream repository: https://github.com/Jeromeyluck/CodeMixBench
Upstream authors:    Yilun Yang, Yekun Chai

Security patch (does not change behaviour or license status): `utils.py` and
`test_model.py` had three `eval()` calls replaced with `ast.literal_eval()`,
`utils.py`'s `load_dataset_from_hf` gained an optional `revision` argument so
the Hub fetch can be pinned to a commit (default `None` keeps the original
behaviour), and `requirements.txt` had three pins raised to their patched
releases: `scikit_learn` 1.0.2 -> 1.5.0 (CVE-2024-5206), `datasets` 2.18.0 ->
5.0.1 (CVE-2026-66007) and `tqdm` 4.66.2 -> 4.66.3 (CVE-2024-34062). See
docs/DEVIATIONS.md item 11 for the rationale and docs/SECURITY.md for the full
dependency posture -- the files are otherwise byte-identical to upstream.

`prompt.json` is upstream benchmark data. This fork reads the prompt templates
from it verbatim so that prompting stays identical to the published benchmark;
it is not modified.


3. Dataset -- Apache License 2.0
--------------------------------
    https://huggingface.co/datasets/CodeMixBench/CodeMixBench

Declared license on the dataset card: apache-2.0.

The dataset is NOT vendored into this repository. It is downloaded at runtime by
`scripts/download_data.py` into `data/raw/` (gitignored). Note that the
CodeMixBench splits are themselves adapted from prior corpora (LinCE, GLUECoS,
MMLU, GSM8K, TruthfulQA, and several Dravidian code-mixed sentiment datasets);
if you redistribute derived data, check the terms of those upstream sources too.


4. Model weights
----------------
Every model evaluated here carries its own license, several of which are NOT
OSI-approved and restrict redistribution or commercial use (e.g. the Gemma Terms
of Use, the Llama Community License). No weights are included in this
repository. Consult each model card before publishing results or derivatives.


